## High-risk surfaces to watch in future work

### `initModel()`

Sensitive because it owns explicit lifecycle semantics, duplicate-init rejection, config override behavior, effective config planning, and attempt identity. Avoid adding async work before `initInProgress` is set.

### `ensureModelReady()`

Sensitive because prompt auto-init must not silently override or bypass failed explicit custom/profile init. It must also not compete with explicit init options.

### `resetModel()`

Sensitive because it must preserve last winning effective config after hardware-aware init. It should not fall back to defaults after custom/profile init unless explicitly designed.

### Worker `activeConfig`

The worker now uses config snapshots. Future changes must be clear about whether they change static imported config, effective parent config, or worker active config.

### Test contract drift

After hardware-aware branch, old Init Retry v1 tests are not current contract. Always run current tests:

```bash
node ./tests/smokeTestHardwareAwareInitRetry.mjs
node ./tests/smokeTestLifecycleRegression.mjs
```

### Config shape verification

Always verify `config.mjs` keeps this shape:

```js
export const config = {
  modelLoad: { ... },
  context: { ... },
  model: { ... },
  runtime: { ... },
  sessions: { ... },
  stream: { ... }
};
```

The worker expects `config.context.*` / effectiveConfig context shape. Flattening context fields is a real regression.

